bacnet-stack 1.6.1 src/bacnet/datalink/bsc/bvlc-sc.c: BVLC-SC 2-octet fields most significant octet first.

1.6.1 copies every 2-octet field (Message ID, Error Class, Error Code, Maximum BVLC Length, Maximum NPDU
Length, header option Header Length, Vendor Identifier) with memcpy() in host byte order: least significant
octet first on the ESP32-S3. ASHRAE 135 Annex AB (as quoted at bvlc-sc.c:442 and :1634), bacpypes3 and
Wireshark use most significant octet first. This patch encodes and decodes those fields with bacnet-stack's
own encode_unsigned16() / decode_unsigned16() (bacint.c), which also stops the size_t copy into the 2-octet
Header Length of bvlc_sc_encode_proprietary_option(). Upstream master still has the memcpy() (decision 168);
draft report: docs/reports/bacnet-stack-bvlc-sc-byte-order-issue.md.

Applied at configure time by tools/apply_patch.py (strict: every hunk must match) into the build directory;
firmware/components/st_bacnet/CMakeLists.txt compiles that copy. The submodule is not edited (decision 4).
Checked by tests/run_bsc_host_tests.ps1 (vectors vs tools/sc/vectors/bvlc_sc_vectors_be.json).

